#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# drazin_inverse

#% text
# `drazin_inverse(m)` gives the Drazin inverse of the square matrix `m`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# With `k` the index of `m` (the smallest `k` with `rank(m^k) = rank(m^(k + 1))`) it is `m^k (m^(2k + 1))^+ m^k`.

#% item
# For an invertible matrix it is the inverse; for a matrix of index 1 it is the group inverse.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
drazin_inverse([[1, 2], [0, 0]])
#% output
#= [[1, 2], [0, 0]]

#% cell
drazin_inverse([[1, 1, 0], [0, 1, 1], [0, 0, 0]])
#% output
#= [[1, -1, -2], [0, 1, 1], [0, 0, 0]]

#% cell
drazin_inverse([[2, 0], [0, 4]])
#% output
#= [[1/2, 0], [0, 1/4]]

#% cell
drazin_inverse([[0, 1], [0, 0]])
#% output
#= [[0, 0], [0, 0]]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `pseudo_inverse`, `inverse`, `matrix_power`
